BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interactive Installations Tech Meetup Dec 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T210000
UID:ttl-11177326444737@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the TTLMakerspace for a fun evening of creative tech and 
 user experience design.\n\n Responsive Installations: Using Sensors to Con
 trol the Visuals\n\n Public installations come alive when they react to th
 e people around them. In this three-hour workshop\, you'll learn how to us
 e sensors that detect motion\, distance\, touch and more to drive real-tim
 e animations.\n\n This session bridges code and the physical world. Using 
 a Raspberry Pi and p5.js\, we'll wire up sensors\, read their signals\, an
 d map them to visual parameters such as colour\, motion and scale. By the 
 end\, you'll have a working responsive prototype\, the practical skills to
  build work that responds to its audience\, and a clear path to scaling it
  into a full installation.\n\n What you'll learn: \n\n \n- Wiring sensors 
 to a Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins\n\n- Sending sensor readings from the Pi int
 o a p5.js sketch\n\n- Mapping user interactions to animation and visuals\n
 \n- Tips for making installations reliable in public spaces\n\n \n Who is 
 this workshop for? \n\n Artists and creative technologists who want to cre
 ate interactive installations for public spaces\, such as art festivals\, 
 or experience-based activations for brands. This workshop is designed for 
 beginners with some coding experience. No electronics experience is needed
 .\n\n About the Facillitator \n\n This training will be led by James Eberh
 ardt.\n\n James is a tech-focused developer working at the intersection of
  web\, mobile\, and IoT\, who has led many workshops. James has previously
  provided technical development work for artists' projects and is eager to
  collaborate with artists.\n\n Spots are limited\, get yours before they a
 re gone!\n\n Interesting for: User Experience Design\, Interactive Install
 ations\, Escape Rooms
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/interactive-installations-tech-meetup-d
 ec-2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Practical 3D Print - Jan 4 [Mondays - 6 Week Comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270104T210000
UID:ttl-11174041616577@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go beyond basic 3D 
 printing knowledge and be able to create custom designs. Learn to use CAD 
 modelling to upgrade or build your own models\, optimized for 3D print.\n\
 n \n \n \n \n \n \n Starting with manual printer control\, you will progre
 ss to custom modelling and even advanced techniques such as 3D scanning an
 d reverse engineering.\n\n Schedule: \n\n \n Six three-hour weekly classes
 \, Mondays 6:00pm to 9:00pm.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes: \n \n \n At the 
 end of this course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n \n \n
 - A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from concept to compl
 eted part\n\n- Experience and comprehension of parametric 3D modelling\n\n
 - Knowledge of 3D printing best practices \n\n- Familiarity with scanning
  for 3D print \n\n- Principles of reverse engineering and part repair\n\n
 - Understanding of the properties of different 3D printing filaments\n\n- 
 Use cases for SLA (resin) printing vs. FDM printing \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \
 n \n Following this hands-on course\, you’ll be certified to use 3D prin
 ters and book time with the machines at the TTLMakerspace (with your membe
 rship). You will also be able to join the growing community of TTL Makers 
 sharing 3D printing & 3D modelling knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n
  Useful for: design prototyping\, custom organizational tools\, repairs\, 
 prop-making\, decorations\, fabrication tools\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \
 n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing
  list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/practical-3d-print-jan-4-mondays-6-week
 -comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In-Depth Intro to Woodworking - Jan 3 [Sundays - 6 week Intensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T130000
UID:ttl-11174000853185@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Description: \n\n \n Suitable for beginners\, this woodworkin
 g course is designed to teach you all that you need to get started in wood
 working by learning both traditional\, and modern techniques.\n\n Students
  will learn valuable hands-on skills working on instructor-lead projects u
 sing both hand and power tools.\n\n Projects are chosen to provide skills 
 development in a natural progression from familiarity with the unique char
 acteristics of wood\, to basic essential techniques\, to some more advance
 d topics.\n\n Materials and equipment for all projects are provided with t
 he course.\n\n \n\n Schedule : \n\n Six three-hour weekly classes\, Sunda
 ys 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outcomes : \n\n At the end of this course you will ha
 ve achieved the following goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the 
 nature and properties of wood \n\n- Proficiency with traditional woodworki
 ng techniques\n\n- Comfort working with chisels\, planes\, saws\n\n- Profi
 ciency with wood milling techniques\n\n- Comfort with safe operation of p
 ower tools\n\n- Familiarity with power planing\, joiner\, drill press\, ro
 uter and table saw \n\n- Dressing and laminating wood \n\n- Experience fo
 llowing project plans \n\n- Familiarity with joinery \n\n- Wood finishing\
 , various treatments \n\n \n  Following this course\, you'll be certified
  to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join the growing community of 
 TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n Certifications 
 for all courses are valid for one year from the time that they are issued\
 , and can be renewed at no cost with your active monthly membership within
  3 months of their expiry. Certification renewal requires booking with an 
 instructor\, is conducted at the makerspace\, and helps you keep your skil
 ls current. \n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organisers\, cutting-b
 oards \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n 
 Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-intro-to-woodworking-jan-3-sun
 days-6-week-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
